n the national climate, or escalation of the wage and housing claims against Askar could quickly move this margin.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Florida's 22nd District is an open seat drawn by the state's Republican-led redistricting, with a Republican-leaning electorate but no incumbent on the ballot. Casey Askar has heavily outspent Pia Dandiya, largely through self-funding, while Dandiya has posted strong fundraising quarters and drawn national surrogates including Pete Buttigieg. Outside groups have spent against Askar, who faces questions about wage and housing claims he denies.\n\nWith no recent independent polling, the outlook rests on fundamentals and outside signals. The district's Republican lean is roughly offset by a favorable national environment for Democrats, and prediction markets along with most expert ratings give Dandiya a modest edge. The result is a narrow Democratic advantage with wide uncertainty, in a race both parties treat as winnable.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5493, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5402, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4658, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4995, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5432, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5455, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5764, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5967, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5933, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5824, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.5625, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.5006, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4998, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.5633, "margin": 1.5}, {"dat